; bfsodium SHA_256 EXPAND : one word of the message schedule
;
; HAND WRITTEN skeleton; The rotate  the shift  the exclusive or and the adder
; are each PASTED from their own verified files;
;
; INTERFACE entry=15 exit=0 footprint=0:132
; IO  in:  w0{4} LE  w1{4} LE  w9{4} LE  w14{4} LE     (16 bytes)
;     out: the next schedule word{4} LE                (4 bytes)
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x00:0x03  w0{4}   u32 LE  W{t minus 16}; SPENT
;   @0x04:0x07  w1{4}   u32 LE  W{t minus 15}; SPENT
;   @0x08:0x0b  w9{4}   u32 LE  W{t minus 7};  SPENT
;   @0x0c:0x0f  w14{4}  u32 LE  W{t minus 2};  SPENT
;   @0x10:0x13  out{4}  u32 LE  the answer
;   @0x14:0x27  four scratch words and the temp a copy hands back through
;   @0x30:0x43  the adder frame; add32 footprint 0:19 at @0x30
;   @0x48:0x61  the exclusive or frame; xor32 0:25 at @0x48
;   @0x68:0x74  the rotate frame; rotr32 0:12 at @0x68
;   @0x78:0x84  the shift frame; shr32 0:12 at @0x78
;
; FIPS 180_4 section 6 point 2 point 2 gives the recurrence as
;   W{t} = sigma1(W{t minus 2}) plus W{t minus 7} plus sigma0(W{t minus 15})
;          plus W{t minus 16}
; with sigma0 x = ROTR 7 xor ROTR 18 xor SHR 3
; and  sigma1 x = ROTR 17 xor ROTR 19 xor SHR 10;
;
; The four taps arrive here as four adjacent words because the caller keeps a
; sliding window of sixteen and they sit at fixed places in it; that is why
; this routine needs no index and takes no position;
;
; Note that the two small sigmas mix rotations with a genuine SHIFT  which is
; the only reason idiom/shr32 exists at all;

; read the four taps
,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,
; ASSERT ptr=15
; ASSERT zero 16:132

; ==== sigma0 of W{t minus 15} ====
; the word into the rotate frame
L11
  [-R100+L68+L32]
R1
  [-R100+L68+L32]
R1
  [-R100+L68+L32]
R1
  [-R100+L68+L32]
; and the temp hands the original straight back
R29
  [-L32+R32]
R1
  [-L32+R32]
R1
  [-L32+R32]
R1
  [-L32+R32]
R69
; the rotation count
  +++++++
L4
; ASSERT ptr=104
@@ROTR32@@ 104
; ASSERT ptr=104
; the rotated word comes back
